<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Once a party is booked, its page has a <strong>Print</strong> card. Each button opens the document in a new tab,
        ready to print.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="The documents">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Reserved table card</strong>: folds in half so the child's name reads from both sides of the table.</li>
            <li><strong>Hot food sheet</strong> or <strong>Cold food sheet</strong>, depending on the party's food. The hot sheet has
                the party details and allergy notes at the top, then every meal with its allergens and a row per side to tally.
                The cold sheet has a row per child for their sandwich choice and an allergy panel.</li>
            <li><strong>Free return voucher</strong>: for the birthday child, with the party date, an expiry date and
                "Authorised by" with the name of whoever prints it.</li>
            <li><strong>Feedback form</strong>: for the parent, with the party name and host filled in.</li>
            <li><strong>Print everything</strong> puts them all in one document.</li>
        </ul>
        <HelpNote>
            The food sheets are only as good as the menu: set the meals, sides and sandwiches, with their allergens, in
            <a href="/manage/parties/settings">Party Settings</a> first.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
